Problem: Search a 2D Matrix (LC 74)

Pattern: Binary Search (Virtual 1D Array)

Approach:

Find the number of rows and columns.
Treat the matrix as a single sorted array.
Initialize:
left = 0
right = rows * cols - 1
While left <= right:
Find mid.
Convert mid to 2D indices:
row = mid / cols
col = mid % cols
Compare matrix[row][col] with target.
If equal → return true.
If smaller → search right half.
If larger → search left half.
If the loop ends, return false.

Time Complexity: O(log(rows × cols))

Space Complexity: O(1)